Z||000000||Shiner||12-30-1999||02:55 AM||||I am going to be totally restoring my '87 GT 5speed over the winter/spring.  Right now, the car has a very faded gold repaint (originaly gold), silver ground effects, and repainted gold wheels (originaly grey).  Oh, and a tan interior.  Here is what I am thinking; Rosa red (arrest me red, whatever you want to call it) all around, like an '88, painting the mirrors to match, keeping the black trim, and repainting the wheels bright gold.  What do you think?  This scheme with the tan interior looks terrific.  But what do all you guys out there in fiero la-la land think?  Keep it stock color?  Repaint like an '88, or repaint (any color) and keep the silver ground effects?  I want to hear you!||||reg||4
Z||000001||2FAST4U||12-30-1999||08:46 AM||||Fieros look good painted any color under the rainbow as long as it's red.<BR>What I'm trying to say is - paint it red.<BR>and if you don't like that color then paint it red.||||reg||1
