Z||000009||Phil||12-30-1999||06:05 PM||||If you are actually RESTORING it you must keep the original factory paint scheme. If you are REPAIRING it anything goes.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BigBoyToys||12-30-1999||08:14 PM||||Keep the Chassis Gold, wheel centers Black, ground effects full wrap Black, side molding leave Black, wing Black, mirrors Black, tint windows Gold (or Black), if you use a nose cover (bra) paint headlight doors Black. <P>I just bought a White 86GT with the Grey ground effects this past fall and a 84 Grey SE for parts, my plan is to put the grey sunroof panel, headlight doors and hood (with some scoop mods) on the GT, tint the windows Black and maybe paint the wing and decklid Grey or just the wing Black. If I don't like the three tone effect it will all be 88 type white with tinted windows. Just my 2 cents so I guess that makes it 6 cents. Mike ||||reg||1
Z||000011||BENGAL4||12-30-1999||08:41 PM||||I vote for orange with black stripes. Sammy Hagar votes for RED.||||reg||14
Z||000012||RFMike||12-30-1999||08:49 PM||||This may seem boring to those of you that prefer the wild color schemes, but I prefer the black body with grey ground effects.  I looked forever for the GT I have because of this preference.  The black side moldings look like they are part of the design with the black field color.  I guess I'm conservative, but in ten years, this scheme will still look great.<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000013||M King||12-30-1999||11:36 PM||||I would have to say that stock red with silver/gray ground effects is my fav color on fieros. I think gold is nice also, but red is still my favorite. I think this is one of the best looking fieros I have ever seen. And I really like the wheels!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierowayne.com/fierojuly.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierowayne.com/fierojuly.jpg</A> <p>[This message has been edited by M King (edited 12-30-1999).]||||reg||3
Z||000014||HotFieroGT||12-31-1999||10:27 PM||||Hey shiner,<P>I would do what you are doing also, I have a red 88GT with the black wheels on it and would kind of like the gold ones.  But the ultimate Fiero is the black 88GT on the cover of the FOCOA magazine this quarter!  Black with steamroller tires, lowered, and a 3.1 turbo, it doesn't get any better than that!||||reg||6
Z||000015||theogre||12-31-1999||11:57 PM||||I never liked GM "gold" much. If you want to stay with a "model valid" color for 87 use the blue. If you don't like that blue try either ford "grabber blue" used on a small number of 2 door Maverick, or try AMC "Big Bad Blue". Both are from the 70's. they should be in the better computer mixers. they can also be found in old, very old now, chip books.<P>Grabber Blue is a little lighter than Fiero blue. Big Bad Blue is a little darker. I think I'm going to paint mine BBB. What better than the paint of an extinct car company on an extinct car. Maybe BBB with a trace amount of metal flake. just enough metal to catch an eye.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Phil||01-01-2000||08:13 AM||||If you like blue there is a very nice light met. called Portifino Blue(Ford) color code XC. Women seem to like it very much. My son's 88 GT is that color and he gets compliments all the time. Of course this may interest Ogre more.||||reg||1
Z||000017||87GT||01-01-2000||06:28 PM||||I like white GTs with the tan interior.  I think those are the nicest looking ones of them all.  I also like Black fieros with the gold rims.  I like the maroon on my GT but it is so common.  ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Harry||01-02-2000||02:29 AM||||I have thought this one over many a dreaming night. Considering we both have tan, mine is two tone I was thinking about dark cherry red or maroon with a very small touch of gold metal flake followed up with pearl white rally stripes. With white rallys you could use either wheel color (gold/silver).<BR>For that matter they dont have to be rallys you could use any type of stripping effect.<BR>By now you should about 60 cents worth. ||||reg||6
Z||000019||TwisT||01-02-2000||04:07 PM||||RED<P>Can you say,  "Ferrari-esque???"||||reg||1
Z||000020||Raydar||01-02-2000||05:06 PM||||One of the best looking Fieros I've ever seen was an 86 or 87 gold GT, with the silver ground effects, and gray wheel spokes. Gold GTs are not really common, in my neck of the woods. Most of them seem to be black. In other words, I'd go for the gold. <BR>On the other hand, my Formula (like most) is red. Going to have it repainted with that bright metallic red that Ford (there's that F-word) and Lincoln are using. Can you say "ticket magnet"? ||||reg||1
